cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Snow-Accident Dataset, please cite this dataset and the associated paper."
title: "Snow-Accident Dataset: Accident-Related Object Detection under Adverse Ice-and-Snow Conditions"
type: dataset
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-11

authors:
  - family-names: "Chen"
    given-names: "Guanyu"
    affiliation: "Northeast Forestry University"

abstract: >
  Snow-Accident is a one-class object detection dataset for evaluating
  traffic accident perception under adverse ice-and-snow conditions.
  It provides YOLO-format annotations and predefined training,
  validation, light-degradation, moderate-degradation, heavy-degradation,
  and normal-weather test subsets.

keywords:
  - traffic accident detection
  - object detection
  - adverse weather
  - ice-and-snow conditions
  - intelligent transportation
  - YOLO
  - computer vision
  - visual robustness

